<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Pont-à-Mousson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1572–1768</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Jesuit University of Pont-à-Mousson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of Pont-à-Mousson was founded in 1572 by Duke Charles III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> and his cousin Cardinal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-duke-of-lower-lorraine">Charles of Lorraine</a>, with papal approval, and was run by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>. A centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Catholic Reformation</a> in Lorraine and the neighbouring lands, it taught theology, law and medicine. After the expulsion of the Jesuits it was transferred to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nancy">Nancy</a> in 1768.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-pont-a-mousson.jpg" alt="University of Pont-à-Mousson" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rolf Krahl (Rotkraut) · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moselle_Pont-a-Mousson.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
